  "proof_summary": [
    "The displayed scalar definitions distinguish physical unit affine evaluation from the canonical inverse coordinate. Angle-defect and irrelevant atom slots are zero.",
    "Actual open maps and inverse maps give the two normalized coordinate values in (0,1), so no unwrapped or unnormalized inverse zeroth bound is inserted.",
    "Finite prefix product/composition estimates use one common M, interval width and reciprocal width at most M, forward/inverse positive jets through N+1 and height/reciprocal jets through N.",
    "For Z=CC*M*M^N every direct pullback is bounded by Z; the inverse Jacobian double pullback costs at most Z^2, the source products cost CP*Z^2. The exact common bound is (CP*CC^2)*M^(2*N+2), including N=0."
  ],
  "scope_limits": [
    "This is a numerical input lemma for the actual displayed geometry scalars, not an assertion that arbitrary supplied geometry has material costs.",
